    // All path data uses a 24x24 grid and only M/L/H/V/C/Z commands — the "A"
    // (arc) command is avoided because WPF's Geometry.Parse arc syntax has
    // documented fidelity differences from SVG's. Round shapes use 4 cubic
    // Bezier curves (the standard k = r * 0.5522847 circle approximation)
    // instead. WPF's mini-language otherwise matches SVG path syntax
    // command-for-command (same letters, same relative/absolute case
    // convention), so SVG path data can be dropped in near-verbatim as long
    // as it avoids arcs — confirmed against Microsoft's Path Markup Syntax
    // docs when the "bolt" icon below was swapped for a supplied SVG.
